# The ChalaMob app does not read environment variables, so there is nothing to copy
# or fill in here. This file only explains where the one setting that matters lives:
# the address of the backend server.
#
# It is set in the code, in  src/api/axios.ts :
#
#   export const PRODUCTION_URL = 'https://chalamob-backend.onrender.com/api';
#
# Change that line and rebuild the APK to point the app at a different server.
# Release builds use HTTPS only.
#
# For development against a backend on your own computer, a debug build lets you pick
# an emulator / USB address in the app (login screen -> "Change"):
#   Android emulator          10.0.2.2:3001
#   Phone on a USB cable      127.0.0.1:3001   (and: adb reverse tcp:3001 tcp:3001)
#   Phone on the same Wi-Fi   <your computer's IP>:3001
#
# The backend has its own settings: see ../crm_backend/.env.example
